...@../../../dev/d2/themes/sequence
# W09: late positive response can win only while original live premises remain valid.
shape: sequence_diagram
coord: Fenced coordinator
issuer: Grant authority
ledger: Admission ledger
broker: Rust broker
cancel: Authorized abort task
coord -> ledger: Retain the durable ConsumePending\nKeep the exact original command
coord -> issuer: Consume the exact original grant
issuer -> issuer: Consume once
coord -> coord: Retain holds after timeout\nDo not infer success
cancel -> cancel: Wait to run the requested abort
issuer -> coord: Return a late authenticated success
coord -> ledger: Try the original S4 CAS\nCheck source, versions, lineage and fence
ledger -> coord: Commit SendCommitted before abort
broker -> coord: Request a claim\nIts premises must still hold
coord -> ledger: Try the unique S5 claim CAS
ledger -> coord: Record the claim as durably spent
coord -> broker: Issue the original one-use send handle
cancel -> ledger: Try AbortNoDispatch CAS\nNo claim may exist
ledger -> cancel: Refuse abort: the claim exists\nDo not refund or reopen the attempt
broker -> broker: Apply the final transport gate\nA claim does not guarantee a send
ledger.rule: "S4 alone does not defeat abort; the S5 claim must win too.\nAn abort between S4 and S5 prevents a claim and a send handle.\nA late callback cannot commit after its premises or original owner change."

# Shared role accents; brand marks are confined to architecture headers.
coord.class: runtime
issuer.class: policy
ledger.class: ledger
broker.class: runtime
cancel.class: deny
ledger.rule.class: note

